.TH VIGIL-ASK 1 2026-11-01 "VIGIL OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vigil-ask \- ask a quick question from the desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vigil-ask
.RB [ window ]
.RB [ \-\-selection ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-history
.IR ID " | " \-\-last ]
.RB [ \-\-stdin ]
.br
.B vigil-ask prompt
.br
.B vigil-ask history
.br
.B vigil-ask ask
.RB [ \-\-selection ]
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-resume
.IR ID ]
.RI [ QUESTION ...| \- ]
.br
.B vigil-ask status
.RB [ \-\-follow ]
.RB [ \-\-polybar ]
.br
.B vigil-ask cancel
.br
.B vigil-ask signin
.br
.B vigil-ask signout
.SH DESCRIPTION
VIGIL Ask answers quick questions in a small window shared by the Plasma and i3 editions.
Questions and anything attached to them go to VIGIL GLM at \fIhttps://chat.vigilglm.ai\fR and are answered in the cloud by GLM models from Z.ai.
You connect VIGIL Ask to your VIGIL GLM account in your browser, and each answer uses that account's credits, within its plan's 5-hour and weekly limits.
There is no API key to create, and VIGIL Ask never sees your password.
.PP
VIGIL Ask asks without web search, images or other tools.
It can answer, but it cannot run commands, read or change files, or browse.
.PP
Nothing is collected in the background.
The selection and files are attached only when you ask for them, and you see each attachment before anything is sent.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B window
Open the window, or bring the open one forward.
\fB\-\-selection\fR attaches the primary selection, \fB\-\-file\fR attaches a UTF-8 text file of up to 512 KiB,
\fB\-\-history\fR reopens a conversation from history and \fB\-\-last\fR the most recent one.
\fB\-\-stdin\fR asks the question read from standard input.
.TP
.B prompt
Ask through a Rofi prompt and show the answer in the window.
.TP
.B history
Pick a recent conversation in Rofi.
.TP
.B ask
Ask in the terminal and print the answer as it arrives. The conversation ID is printed last, for \fB\-\-resume\fR.
Sign in first, with \fBsignin\fR or from the window.
.TP
.B status
Print idle, working, done, stopped, failed, signin or off. It never includes question text.
.TP
.B cancel
Stop the question being answered, in the window or in a terminal. The i3 edition runs this before locking and when you log out.
.TP
.B signin
Connect this computer to a VIGIL GLM account. It prints an address and a code; open the address in any browser, sign in and enter the code.
This works over SSH too. Ctrl+C gives up.
.TP
.B signout
Stop the active answer, delete this computer's VIGIL GLM tokens and ask VIGIL GLM to end the connection. If VIGIL GLM can't be reached,
remove the connection under Settings > Accounts > Connected desktops on VIGIL GLM. The window's \fBSign out\fR button does the same.
.TP
.B krunner
Answer \fBask\fR queries from KRunner. D-Bus starts it when KRunner needs it, and it leaves after ten idle minutes.
.SH DESKTOP
On i3, Super+Shift+A asks through Rofi and Super+Ctrl+A opens the window with the selection attached.
The Polybar module shows the status; click it to ask, middle-click for history and right-click to reopen the last conversation.
In Thunar, \fBSend To\fR > \fBVIGIL Ask\fR attaches the selected text files.
.PP
On Plasma, Meta+Alt+A opens the window and Meta+Alt+Shift+A opens it with the selection attached.
Change them in System Settings > Keyboard > Shortcuts.
In KRunner, type \fBask\fR and a question; KRunner keeps its own history of what you type there.
Locking the screen stops the answer, in the window or in a terminal.
.PP
In Dolphin, on either edition, \fBActions\fR > \fBAsk VIGIL about this file\fR attaches the selected text files.
.SH FIRST USE
Before the first question the window explains where questions go.
\fBSign in\fR then shows a short code and opens \fIhttps://chat.vigilglm.ai/desktop/verify\fR in your browser.
Sign in there with email, Google or GitHub, or create a free account, enter the code and choose \fBConnect VIGIL Ask\fR.
Only approve a code that VIGIL Ask showed you.
The connection can ask text questions with the account's credits, read its name and email and show usage; nothing else.
If the connection ends or is revoked, the window asks you to sign in again and keeps the pending question and attachments.
The window shows the account and how much of its limits is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vigil-ask/config.json
\fBenabled\fR (true), \fBhistory_days\fR (30; 0 keeps no history), \fBmodel\fR (glm-5.3-flash when null, or glm-5.3),
\fBeffort\fR (low when null, high or max) and \fBnotice_accepted\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/vigil-ask/history.json
Recent questions and answers, readable only by you.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/vigil-ask/session.json
This computer's VIGIL GLM tokens, readable only by you. Anyone who can read them can ask questions on your account's credits
until the connection is revoked, so treat the file like a password.
.TP
.I /etc/vigil-ask/disabled
When this file exists, VIGIL Ask is off for every user.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fIhttps://chat.vigilglm.ai/legal/privacy\fR, \fIhttps://chat.vigilglm.ai/usage\fR
